      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks. This is a good start on the actual content/critique. \n\nHowever, the structural thoroughness score for this draft came back way too low. It's basically just one block. I know I told you not to pad it with fluff, but for a Nature-level review, I really need it to look more comprehensive and multi-faceted. \n\nCan you expand this into a more formal, structured review? Break down the critique into the specific methodological areas we discussed (sample prep, the annealing process, the EPR spectroscopy, the SNR, etc.). Just make sure the sections are substantive—I'll be checking to make sure you aren't just adding empty headings to pump the score.",
